{"slug":"diagnostics","number":"10","title":"Validation and diagnostics","file":"spec/core/10-diagnostics.md","sections":[{"id":"10.1","number":"10.1","title":"Validity"},{"id":"10.2","number":"10.2","title":"Diagnostics"},{"id":"10.3","number":"10.3","title":"Order of evaluation"},{"id":"10.4","number":"10.4","title":"Catalogue"},{"id":"10.5","number":"10.5","title":"Fix operations"}],"blocks":[{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"10.1","number":"10.1","c":["Validity"]},{"t":"p","c":["Validation runs in tiers:"]},{"t":"list","ordered":true,"start":0,"items":[[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Configuration"]}," — are the known extensions the validator is configured with a valid registry (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/extensions#12.2","c":["12.2"]},")? (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-CFG-"},")"]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Parsing"]}," — is it JSON, as ",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/serialization#9.1","c":["9.1"]}," requires? (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-JSON-"},")"]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Document"]}," — can this reader read it at all: its version and its required extensions? (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-DOC-"},")"]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Schema"]}," — does it match the JSON Schema of the draft it declares? (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-SCH-"},")"]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Invariants"]}," — the rules no schema can express: references resolve, the wall graph is planar, rooms, openings, hosted elements, floors, ceilings and roofs fit, the program is consistent, the extensions known to the validator are used as their registry entries say, and stairs rise between two levels of a building; a texture's maps are images and a wall's finish regions fit its faces; and, for a package validator, every packaged asset's file is there and is the file its asset names (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/materials#18.4","c":["18.4"]},") — and, in a document with design options, no reference crosses options and every checked design is valid (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/options#19.5","c":["19.5"]},"). (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-"},")"]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Lints"]}," — conditions that make a valid document worse. (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-"},")"]}]]},{"t":"p","c":["The schema is applied to the parsed document, in which a number written with a fraction or an exponent is not an integer: ",{"t":"code","v":"1.0"}," is not a length. A document that declares ",{"t":"code","v":"\"0.1\""},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"0.2\""}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"0.3\""}," is checked against that draft's schema (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/model#FS-CORE-1.2.8","c":["1.2.8"]},"); every other document reaching the schema tier, against this draft's."]},{"t":"p","c":["A document is ",{"t":"strong","c":["valid"]}," when the first five tiers, 0 to 4, report no error. Lints never make a document invalid."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-10.1.1","level":"MUST","c":["A validator MUST report a document as valid if, and only if, it reports no diagnostic with severity ",{"t":"code","v":"error"},"."]}]},{"t":"p","c":["A model that violates any invariant is invalid; an edit that would produce one is rejected, and the document is left unchanged (Floorspec Ops)."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"10.2","number":"10.2","c":["Diagnostics"]},{"t":"p","c":["A ",{"t":"strong","c":["diagnostic"]}," is a JSON object:"]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null],"head":[["Member"],["Type"],["Meaning"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"code"}],["string"],["the stable code from the catalogue (",{"t":"a","href":"#10.4","c":["10.4"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"severity"}],[{"t":"code","v":"\"error\""},", ",{"t":"code","v":"\"warning\""}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"\"info\""}],["as the catalogue gives it"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"message"}],["string"],["a human-readable explanation; its wording is not normative"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"elements"}],["array of IDs, sorted"],["the elements involved, as the catalogue lists them"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"location"}],["object"],["where: any of ",{"t":"code","v":"pointer"}," (a JSON Pointer, RFC 6901, into the document), ",{"t":"code","v":"level"}," (an ID) and ",{"t":"code","v":"point"}," (a point on that level)"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"fix"}],["array of fix operations"],["optional: a change that would clear the diagnostic (",{"t":"a","href":"#10.5","c":["10.5"]},")"]],[[{"t":"code","v":"design"}],["an option's ID"],["present only for a diagnostic found in that option's design, and not in the primary design (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/options#19.5","c":["19.5"]},")"]]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-10.2.1","level":"MUST","c":["A validator MUST report each condition the catalogue lists as a diagnostic with the catalogued code, severity and elements."]}]},{"t":"p","c":["A condition that occurs several times is reported once for each occurrence: once for each unresolved reference, each undeclared extension name, each pair of crossing edges, each pair of coincident junctions, each missing or out-of-range dependency, each missing fallback part. A validator reports diagnostics sorted by code and then by ",{"t":"code","v":"elements"},", compared as sequences of strings, and then by ",{"t":"code","v":"design"},", a diagnostic without one first. For schema violations the catalogue lists a single code, ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-SCH-001"},"; validators differ in how they break a schema violation into parts, so what is compared is only that at least one ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-SCH-001"}," is reported."]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"10.3","number":"10.3","c":["Order of evaluation"]},{"t":"p","c":["A tier only makes sense when the one before it passed: a dangling reference makes \"is this wall graph planar?\" unanswerable. Each tier is evaluated only when every earlier tier reported no error, with these refinements inside tier 4:"]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Configuration"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-CFG-001"},") is evaluated before every tier, parsing included. If it is reported, nothing else is evaluated."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Reference invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-001"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-009"},") are evaluated first. If any is reported, no other invariant is evaluated."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Option invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1101"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1102"},") are evaluated next, of the document as a whole. If any is reported, no other invariant is evaluated. Every invariant below is evaluated for the view of each checked design (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/options#19.5","c":["19.5"]},"), as this section orders it; a document with no option set has one, the document itself."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Program invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-401"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-403"},") are evaluated for every adjacency, except that ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-402"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-403"}," are not evaluated for an adjacency that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-401"},"."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Extension invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-601"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-605"},") are evaluated for every extension the document uses at a version at which it is known (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/extensions#12.2","c":["12.2"]},")."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Hosting invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-501"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-506"},") are evaluated for every extension element and every type, except that ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-502"}," is not evaluated for a host wall that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-112"},", and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-503"}," is evaluated only for a ",{"t":"code","v":"surface"}," host whose room is on a level where room invariants are evaluated and has none of ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-201"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-204"},"."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Graph invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-101"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-108"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-111"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-113"},") are evaluated for every level and wall, except that ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-111"}," is not evaluated for a junction with a wall that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-107"}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-108"},": without layers there are no face lines to compare. An arc edge whose arc does not fit (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-113"},", evaluated for every arc edge without ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-102"},") has no polyline (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/arcs#21.2","c":["21.2"]},"), so ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-104"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-106"}," are not evaluated for it, and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-111"}," is not evaluated for a junction it ends at."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Join invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-109"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-110"},") and ",{"t":"strong","c":["room invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-201"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-204"},") are evaluated only for levels on which no graph invariant other than ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-112"}," was reported."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Opening and type invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-301"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-308"},") are evaluated for every opening and every door or window type, except that ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-303"}," is not evaluated for an opening whose wall has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-112"},", and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-302"}," not for one on an arc wall with ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-102"}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-113"},", which has no length (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/arcs#21.6","c":["21.6"]},"); nor are ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-501"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1002"}," for such a wall."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Floor and ceiling invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-701"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-703"},") are evaluated only for a room on a level where room invariants are evaluated, and that has none of ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-201"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-204"},": they are tested on its room polygon. ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-701"}," is not evaluated for a room that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-702"},": a vault without a ridge line has no elevation."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Roof invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-801"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-805"},") are evaluated for every roof, except that ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-805"}," is not evaluated for a roof that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-804"},": its moved lines need not meet."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Stair invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-901"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-906"},") are evaluated for every stair, except that ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-902"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-903"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-906"}," are evaluated only for a stair without ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-901"}," whose two levels are levels where room invariants are evaluated and have no room with any of ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-201"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-204"}," — its rise, and so its riser count, is measured from its rooms' floors (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/stairs#17.4","c":["17.4"]},") — ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-903"}," is not evaluated for a stair that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-902"},", and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-906"}," is not evaluated for a stair that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-902"}," or ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-903"},": the angles of its treads divide its turn or its sweep among the treads its riser count gives it (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/stairs#17.7","c":["17.7"]},")."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Material and finish invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1001"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1004"},") are evaluated for every material and every region of every wall's finishes, except that ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1002"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1003"}," are not evaluated for a region that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1001"},", and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1002"}," does not test a region's ",{"t":"code","v":"top"}," on a wall that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-112"},"."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Package invariants"]}," (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1005"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1007"},") are evaluated only by a package validator (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/materials#18.4","c":["18.4"]},"), for every asset located by ",{"t":"code","v":"path"},", except that ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1006"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1007"}," are not evaluated for an asset that has ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-INV-1005"},"."]}],[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Lints"]}," are evaluated only for a valid document: ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-006"},", ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-007"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-017"}," of the document as a whole, and every other lint for the view of each checked design. The circulation lints (",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-012"}," to ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-014"},") are evaluated only for a building that is evaluated (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/circulation#14.4","c":["14.4"]},"), and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-012"}," and ",{"t":"code","v":"FS-LINT-013"}," only for a building that has an entry (",{"t":"a","href":"/floorspec/core/circulation#14.2","c":["14.2"]},")."]}]]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"stmt","id":"FS-CORE-10.3.1","level":"MUST NOT","c":["A validator MUST NOT report a diagnostic that this section says is not evaluated."]}]},{"t":"h","depth":2,"id":"10.4","number":"10.4","c":["Catalogue"]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"strong","c":["Parsing and document."]}]},{"t":"table","align":[null,null,null,null,null],"head":[["Code"],["Severity"],["Condition"],["Elements"],["Rule"]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","v":"FS-CFG-001"}],["error"],["the validator's known extensions are not a valid registry: an entry does not match the registry entry schema, two en